Subject: [PATCH] qemu: give each help request its own output

inspectFeatures runs `qemu -accel help`, `-netdev help`, `-machine help` and
`-cpu help` into the same two buffers, and keeps each output as the buffer's
Bytes() after its run. NetdevHelp is the accelerators' text followed by the
netdevs', MachineHelp has both and its own, CPUHelp all four. The features
are searched as text (strings.Contains): a word of an earlier help can match
a later one's feature.

Each request has its own buffers now (qemuHelp).

Test: TestInspectFeaturesOwnOutputs.

---
